@* The API documentation page (ApiDocs.razor), part 2: after the start. Follow the review, read the report, cancel
   it. Each call is laid out the same way (Jakob's law): the method and address, what to send, the request and the
   answer right under it (proximity). A section never relies on another: the edit key's header is named again. *@

<section id="follow" class="mt-12 scroll-mt-6" aria-labelledby="follow-title">
    <h2 id="follow-title" class="font-display text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-heading">Follow it</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 font-mono text-[15px]">
        <span class="border border-heading px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide text-heading">GET</span>
        <span class="break-all text-heading">/api/v1/reviews/{id}</span>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4">
        Ask for the status every 30 seconds or so. No key is needed. The <code class="@Code">stage</code> tells you where
        the review is, and <code class="@Code">step</code> counts up from 1 to 7. When the stage is Complete, the answer
        also holds the verdicts and the links to the files.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock Id="status-request" Label="Request" Code="@AuBtechReviewAgent.ApiDocExamples.StatusCurl(BaseUrl)" />
    <CodeBlock Id="status-answer" Label="200 OK" Code="@AuBtechReviewAgent.ApiDocExamples.Status(BaseUrl)" />
    <p class="mt-4">
        A review ends as Complete, Failed or Cancelled. If it did not complete, <code class="@Code">failure</code> says why.
    </p>
</section>

<section id="report" class="mt-12 scroll-mt-6" aria-labelledby="report-title">
    <h2 id="report-title" class="font-display text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-heading">Read the report</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 font-mono text-[15px]">
        <span class="border border-heading px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide text-heading">GET</span>
        <span class="break-all text-heading">/api/v1/reviews/{id}/report</span>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4">
        Once the stage is Complete, ask for the report. You get the title, the abstract and each section as text. You
        also get each citation with its verdict and the quote it was checked against, the reference list and the PRISMA
        counts. Nothing is written for you: it is read from the review's own files.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock Id="report-request" Label="Request" Code="@AuBtechReviewAgent.ApiDocExamples.ReportCurl(BaseUrl)" />
    <CodeBlock Id="report-answer" Label="200 OK, with one item in each list" Code="@AuBtechReviewAgent.ApiDocExamples.Report" />
</section>

<section id="cancel" class="mt-12 scroll-mt-6" aria-labelledby="cancel-title">
    <h2 id="cancel-title" class="font-display text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-heading">Cancel it</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 font-mono text-[15px]">
        <span class="border border-heading px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide text-heading">DELETE</span>
        <span class="break-all text-heading">/api/v1/reviews/{id}</span>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4">
        Send the edit key in the <code class="@Code">X-Edit-Key</code> header. It came back in the answer when you
        started the review. You may add a reason to the address, and it is kept on file.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock Id="cancel-request" Label="Request" Code="@AuBtechReviewAgent.ApiDocExamples.CancelCurl(BaseUrl)" />
    <CodeBlock Id="cancel-answer" Label="202 Accepted" Code="@AuBtechReviewAgent.ApiDocExamples.Cancelled(BaseUrl)" />
    <p class="mt-4">
        The answer is 202, not 200. A review that waits in line stops at once. A running review stops at its next safe
        point, and its stage then turns to Cancelled.
    </p>
</section>

@code {
    /// <summary>The address of this server, for the examples.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string BaseUrl { get; set; } = "";

    private const string Code = ApiDocsStart.Code;
}
